{"status": "progress", "message": "Retrieved 122 candidate paragraphs; kept 3", "stage": "retrieve", "claim_index": 1, "data": {"kind": "retrieval", "pass": 1, "queries": ["James Webb Space Telescope", "Lagrange point"], "candidates": 122, "by_source": {"web": 3, "arxiv": 6, "wikipedia": 113}, "avgdl": 118.5, "top": [{"text": "The James Webb Space Telescope orbits the Sun near Sun-Earth Lagrange point 2 (L2), approximately 1.5 million kilometers (1 million miles) from Earth. L2 is one", "source": "web", "dense": 0.871, "bm25": 22.4, "dense_rank": 1, "bm25_rank": 1, "rrf": 0.03279, "selected": true}, {"text": "Webb orbits the Sun near the second Lagrange point (L2) of the Sun-Earth system, which is 1,500,000 km (930,000 mi) farther from the Sun than the Earth's orbit,", "source": "web", "dense": 0.757, "bm25": 21.5, "dense_rank": 3, "bm25_rank": 2, "rrf": 0.032, "selected": true}, {"text": "A Solar Orbit The James Webb Space Telescope is not in orbit around the Earth, like the Hubble Space Telescope is - it actually orbits the Sun, 1.5 million kilo", "source": "web", "dense": 0.84, "bm25": 18.87, "dense_rank": 2, "bm25_rank": 3, "rrf": 0.032, "selected": true}, {"text": "Several planets have trojan asteroids near their L4 and L5 points with respect to the Sun; Jupiter has more than one million of these trojans. Some Lagrange poi", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.704, "bm25": 16.46, "dense_rank": 4, "bm25_rank": 4, "rrf": 0.03125, "selected": false}, {"text": "Examples of spacecraft designed to operate near the Earth\u2013Sun L2 are the Webb and Roman space telescopes. Earlier examples include the Wilkinson Microwave Aniso", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.702, "bm25": 14.15, "dense_rank": 5, "bm25_rank": 6, "rrf": 0.03054, "selected": false}, {"text": "The Deep Space Climate Observatory (DSCOVR), an artificial satellite, is located at L1 to study solar wind coming toward Earth from the Sun and to monitor Earth", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.671, "bm25": 14.39, "dense_rank": 7, "bm25_rank": 5, "rrf": 0.03031, "selected": false}, {"text": "Despite Webb's mirror diameter being 2.7 times larger than that of the Hubble Space Telescope, it produces images of comparable resolution because it observes i", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.679, "bm25": 11.14, "dense_rank": 6, "bm25_rank": 17, "rrf": 0.02814, "selected": false}, {"text": "In January 2022, it arrived at its destination, a solar orbit near the Sun\u2013Earth L2 Lagrange point, about 1.5 million kilometers (930,000 mi) from Earth. The te", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.643, "bm25": 11.09, "dense_rank": 8, "bm25_rank": 18, "rrf": 0.02753, "selected": false}], "selected": 3, "echo_filtered": 0, "kept": 3}, "t": 9.094}
